# ==============================================================================
# GeckoPod-ModZ: CrossLink-NX LIFCL-17 QFN72 Physical Constraints
# Target device: LIFCL-17-6SG72C (CrossLink-NX, QFN72)
#
# STATUS: REV-A LOGICAL CONSTRAINT TEMPLATE — NOT PCB-AUTHORITATIVE
#
# This file intentionally contains NO guessed package-site assignments.
# Populate ldc_set_location only from Lattice's official LIFCL-17 QFN72 pinout,
# package-DD, and D-PHY documentation after bank/power verification.
# Timing constraints belong in lifcl17_revA.sdc.
# ==============================================================================

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. System clock and reset
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18} [get_ports clk_sys]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP} [get_ports rst_n]

# TODO after official pin-map verification:
# ldc_set_location -site {<CLOCK_CAPABLE_SITE>} [get_ports clk_sys]
# ldc_set_location -site {<USER_IO_SITE>}       [get_ports rst_n]

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. iPod 5G/5.5G LCD parallel bus — 1.8 V
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_wr_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_cs_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=DOWN} [get_ports ipod_rs]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_rd_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports ipod_reset_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=DOWN} [get_ports {ipod_db[*]}]

# Physical-placement goals:
#   - Keep DB[15:0] physically compact.
#   - Place controls in the same compatible 1.8-V I/O region when practical.
#   - Preserve all fixed D-PHY resources and configuration pins.
#   - Confirm the selected VCCIO rails are actually powered at 1.8 V.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. AMOLED panel sideband control — nominal 1.8 V logic
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=UP}   [get_ports panel_reset_n]
ldc_set_port -iobuf {IO_TYPE=LVCMOS18 PULLMODE=DOWN} [get_ports panel_te]

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. MIPI D-PHY / DSI
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT assign arbitrary package sites here.
# CrossLink-NX hardened D-PHY lane locations are fixed by the selected D-PHY
# quad / IP configuration and must match Lattice's official pin mapping.
#
# The exact generated-IP wrapper may also dictate port names and I/O attributes.
# Keep these logical names only as the project-facing interface until the
# D-PHY/DSI IP configuration is frozen.
#
# Logical ports expected by the current board plan:
#   mipi_clk_p / mipi_clk_n
#   mipi_d0_p  / mipi_d0_n
#   mipi_d1_p  / mipi_d1_n
#
# Do NOT assume that setting IO_TYPE=MIPI_DPHY on arbitrary user I/O converts
# them into hardened D-PHY lanes.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Package/power/configuration requirements
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The KiCad symbol and PCB must include every device-required pin from the
# official QFN72 package documentation, including as applicable:
#   - all VCC / core rails
#   - all VCCAUX / auxiliary rails
#   - every VCCIO bank supply
#   - all GND pins and exposed pad
#   - configuration pins
#   - JTAG/programming/debug pins
#   - D-PHY-specific supplies/references
#
# These are device pins, not HDL ports, so they are not represented by
# get_ports statements in this PDC.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 6. Package locations — TODO BEFORE SCHEMATIC/PCB FREEZE
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example syntax ONLY after verification:
# ldc_set_location -site {<OFFICIAL_SITE>} [get_ports ipod_wr_n]
# ldc_set_location -site {<OFFICIAL_SITE>} [get_ports {ipod_db[0]}]
# ldc_set_location -site {<OFFICIAL_SITE>} [get_ports panel_reset_n]
#
# Required verification sources:
#   - LIFCL-17 device pinout
#   - QFN72 package / pin-migration data
#   - CrossLink-NX package-DD data
#   - CrossLink-NX hardened D-PHY usage / IP documentation

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 7. RTL naming note
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The capture path is intentionally controller-agnostic. Do not use the earlier
# ipod_s1d19122_capture name as a hardware assumption; the project currently
# uses ipod_bus_capture / trace-parser terminology until the LCD command model
# is verified from real captures.
